-- An erased account's contributor records may go (t1053; GDPR Articles 17(1) and 17(3)(e)). `contributors` is ledger class (0009): it refused every delete, so the record of which account added to a shared total could not be removed, and an erasure could only leave it.
-- The rule now has one exception and no other. A `contributors` row may be deleted when the operator's account erasure has already written a tombstone of kind `account` for the row's account (`digest` holds the pool's own pseudonymous account id there, the same id `erasure_audit` already keeps). Nothing else lifts it: the Worker writes no tombstone, and the tombstones are append-only (0018).
DROP TRIGGER contributors_no_delete;
CREATE TRIGGER contributors_no_delete BEFORE DELETE ON contributors WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM erasure_tombstones WHERE kind = 'account' AND digest = OLD.account) BEGIN SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'ledger rows are never deleted'); END;
